<title>USA: Lockheed part of Japan navigation team.</title>
<headline>Lockheed part of Japan navigation team.</headline>
<dateline>GAITHERSBURG, Md. 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lockheed Martin Federal Systems said Monday it has been selected to help design and develop the Japanese government's new global navigation satellite system, the Multifunction Transport Satellite-Based Augmentation System.</p>
<p>The Lockheed Martin Corp subsidiary said it is a member of a team led by NEC Corp.</p>
<p>The award has a potential value of about $36 million, or about 4 billion yen, to the NEC team, Lockheed said.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
